1
00:00:03,946 --> 00:00:06,376
The baby I had waited for so long,

2
00:00:08,360 --> 00:00:11,490
the baby I considered more precious than my own life,

3
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:16,470
was suddenly taken from me one day.

4
00:00:19,370 --> 00:00:20,870
I resented the world,

5
00:00:21,370 --> 00:00:22,840
and I resented myself.

6
00:00:24,670 --> 00:00:26,140
I blamed myself...

7
00:00:26,810 --> 00:00:28,340
for failing to protect my baby...

8
00:00:30,280 --> 00:00:32,580
and even attempted to take my own life.

9
00:00:35,950 --> 00:00:36,990
And...

10
00:00:39,190 --> 00:00:40,320
all this time,

11
00:00:43,290 --> 00:00:44,930
in order to protect my husband,

12
00:00:47,400 --> 00:00:50,470
I was going to take this secret to my grave.

13
00:00:53,900 --> 00:00:54,900
But today,

14
00:00:57,070 --> 00:00:58,110
I'm gathering my courage...

15
00:01:01,680 --> 00:01:04,880
to reveal the secret I've kept in my heart...

16
00:01:06,620 --> 00:01:08,280
for the past three years.

17
00:01:11,820 --> 00:01:12,820
I...

18
00:01:17,230 --> 00:01:18,900
took medication that my husband gave me...

19
00:01:20,360 --> 00:01:21,630
and lost my baby.

20
00:01:24,900 --> 00:01:27,900
He gave me medication that I should have never taken.

21
00:01:29,640 --> 00:01:30,740
My husband...

22
00:01:32,340 --> 00:01:34,910
is a murderer who killed our baby.

23
00:01:39,880 --> 00:01:40,880
Plaintiff.

24
00:01:43,390 --> 00:01:45,690
Is what you're saying true?

25
00:01:46,120 --> 00:01:47,860
Yes, it is.

26
00:01:51,930 --> 00:01:53,400
Back when I had my miscarriage,

27
00:01:54,660 --> 00:01:57,300
I confirmed it with my doctor at the time.

28
00:01:58,600 --> 00:02:00,670
I found out that the medication my husband gave me then...

29
00:02:01,600 --> 00:02:03,270
was fatal to the fetus...

30
00:02:03,270 --> 00:02:06,040
What is this bullshit? What do you think you're doing?

31
00:02:06,410 --> 00:02:09,950
Defendant, calm down and take your seat.

32
00:02:16,650 --> 00:02:19,160
Investigator, what she's saying right now...

33
00:02:19,160 --> 00:02:20,820
is completely baseless.

34
00:02:20,920 --> 00:02:22,830
I never gave her any such pills.

35
00:02:22,890 --> 00:02:24,930
More importantly,

36
00:02:24,930 --> 00:02:26,830
why would I ever harm my own child?

37
00:02:26,900 --> 00:02:28,570
This is ridiculous, Investigator.

38
00:02:28,570 --> 00:02:29,970
That's not true, Investigator.

39
00:02:32,870 --> 00:02:36,470
- I'm telling the truth. - Hey!

40
00:02:36,540 --> 00:02:37,870
Quiet, please.

41
00:02:43,550 --> 00:02:46,880
We won't be able to continue the investigation today.

42
00:02:47,280 --> 00:02:49,220
We'll reconvene at the next hearing.

43
00:02:52,290 --> 00:02:53,320
Hey, are you out of your mind?

44
00:02:53,760 --> 00:02:55,160
You're supposed to just state the facts,

45
00:02:55,220 --> 00:02:57,260
so why are you making up this insane story?

46
00:02:57,330 --> 00:02:58,330
It's not a story.

47
00:02:59,100 --> 00:03:01,760
Why would I come all this way just to make things up?

48
00:03:01,930 --> 00:03:04,130
What kind of pills are you even saying I gave you?

49
00:03:04,400 --> 00:03:05,570
Do you really not remember?

50
00:03:06,170 --> 00:03:07,600
Pills or whatever else,

51
00:03:07,670 --> 00:03:10,410
I never gave you anything that could have harmed you.

52
00:03:10,810 --> 00:03:14,040
Then maybe you should take this chance to think hard.

53
00:03:15,140 --> 00:03:17,980
Think about if you've only ever given me good things,

54
00:03:17,980 --> 00:03:18,980
pills or otherwise.

55
00:03:19,480 --> 00:03:20,580
Unbelievable.

56
00:03:20,880 --> 00:03:23,050
(Yeonnam Family Court Bulletin)

57
00:03:23,490 --> 00:03:24,490
Fine.

58
00:03:24,550 --> 00:03:27,160
Let's just say you're having some ridiculous delusion for now.

59
00:03:27,790 --> 00:03:29,360
Then why have you been quiet all this time?

60
00:03:29,960 --> 00:03:33,300
Why say nothing until now and then cause a scene here?

61
00:03:34,600 --> 00:03:35,800
I was going to...

62
00:03:37,500 --> 00:03:39,170
just carry this burden alone.

63
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:42,610
I was worried it would be too hard on you.

64
00:03:43,670 --> 00:03:45,580
- But... - But what?

65
00:03:48,110 --> 00:03:49,150
What?

66
00:03:49,450 --> 00:03:51,050
I just don't want to anymore.

67
00:03:52,980 --> 00:03:56,290
I can't wait to see what you'll do to me now.

68
00:03:57,090 --> 00:04:01,920
After all, you were so worried when Hee Ju just took some pills.

69
00:04:08,530 --> 00:04:09,530
Gosh.

70
00:04:12,140 --> 00:04:13,200
Do you really not remember?

71
00:04:16,710 --> 00:04:17,810
(Episode 8)

72
00:04:20,140 --> 00:04:22,010
If what your wife is saying is true,

73
00:04:22,850 --> 00:04:24,550
this is incredibly serious.

74
00:04:25,210 --> 00:04:28,650
My wife said she even got a written statement from her doctor.

75
00:04:29,220 --> 00:04:32,120
But I don't even remember buying any pills myself.

76
00:04:32,290 --> 00:04:34,920
Then you should have asked your wife for more details.

77
00:04:35,020 --> 00:04:37,290
This isn't something you can just ignore.

78
00:04:37,690 --> 00:04:40,430
This is separate from the divorce lawsuit.

79
00:04:40,800 --> 00:04:42,400
This could easily be considered attempted murder.

80
00:04:42,830 --> 00:04:44,170
Attempted murder?

81
00:04:44,730 --> 00:04:46,300
No, then does that mean...

82
00:04:46,370 --> 00:04:49,110
when my wife attacked me with a knife...

83
00:04:49,170 --> 00:04:51,010
It's certainly possible.

84
00:04:51,110 --> 00:04:52,340
If she believes the baby died...

85
00:04:52,410 --> 00:04:54,010
because of the pills you gave her,

86
00:04:54,080 --> 00:04:57,310
she would have been much more emotionally unstable and sensitive.

87
00:04:57,480 --> 00:05:00,280
Well, I'm emotionally unstable too.

88
00:05:00,680 --> 00:05:03,120
I have no idea when or where she'll drop another bombshell,

89
00:05:03,120 --> 00:05:06,060
so my heart is pounding, and I feel like I'm going crazy.

90
00:05:06,690 --> 00:05:09,630
Is that why you were so nervous about your secret relationship...

91
00:05:09,630 --> 00:05:10,930
that you made her sign a written pledge?

92
00:05:11,560 --> 00:05:14,030
How did we get back to talking about that?

93
00:05:14,660 --> 00:05:18,230
Anyway, look into it. If there was a mistake, correct it.

94
00:05:19,140 --> 00:05:20,140
Okay.

95
00:05:21,800 --> 00:05:23,440
And you should probably break up with your girlfriend.

96
00:05:24,170 --> 00:05:25,170
What?

97
00:05:26,040 --> 00:05:28,510
Are you just going to continue this loving relationship?

98
00:05:28,710 --> 00:05:30,610
She's the reason this bombshell dropped in the first place.

99
00:05:32,280 --> 00:05:33,550
Oh, honestly.

100
00:05:45,760 --> 00:05:47,060
Good morning.

101
00:05:48,400 --> 00:05:51,500
Why the long faces? You look like you've seen a ghost.

102
00:05:51,870 --> 00:05:53,800
Don't you have a job?

103
00:05:54,100 --> 00:05:56,110
I mean, you seem pretty free for a weekday morning.

104
00:05:57,810 --> 00:05:59,480
I'm a freelancer.

105
00:05:59,880 --> 00:06:01,240
I take days off when I don't have work.

106
00:06:01,680 --> 00:06:04,180
Today is one of those days.

107
00:06:06,450 --> 00:06:08,350
Oh, can I see your phone for a second?

108
00:06:08,680 --> 00:06:10,620
- What? - Quickly.

109
00:06:13,490 --> 00:06:16,630
My name is Ahn Hee Ju.

110
00:06:17,130 --> 00:06:18,260
Not "miss."

111
00:06:19,900 --> 00:06:22,130
You should save my number, just in case.

112
00:06:22,370 --> 00:06:24,230
So you don't break down my door for no reason.

113
00:06:24,530 --> 00:06:26,940
So her last name is Ahn. Ahn Hee Ju.

114
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:29,440
Oh, honestly. Why are you saving her number?

115
00:06:31,170 --> 00:06:34,280
I'm not going to argue. Get out of this house today.

116
00:06:34,410 --> 00:06:36,950
I'll give you a full refund for the month's rent.

117
00:06:37,080 --> 00:06:39,050
Mom, that's a huge loss for us.

118
00:06:39,150 --> 00:06:40,480
If I get sick from the stress she's causing me,

119
00:06:40,550 --> 00:06:41,550
that'll be an even bigger loss.

120
00:06:42,350 --> 00:06:43,820
You'll be out by the end of the day, right?

121
00:06:44,420 --> 00:06:46,290
- No. - What?

122
00:06:46,960 --> 00:06:50,790
Mother, please don't hate me so much.

123
00:06:51,260 --> 00:06:53,460
You're CEO Ji's mother,

124
00:06:53,460 --> 00:06:55,160
so I'd really like for us to get along.

125
00:06:55,230 --> 00:06:56,230
What?

126
00:06:56,900 --> 00:06:59,240
How dare you call me Mother?

127
00:06:59,400 --> 00:07:01,200
You don't like it?

128
00:07:01,840 --> 00:07:04,310
Then I'll just call you Grandma.

129
00:07:04,510 --> 00:07:06,080
I'm more comfortable with that, actually.

130
00:07:06,940 --> 00:07:08,010
Grandma.

131
00:07:09,380 --> 00:07:10,880
Well, I'll be heading up then.

132
00:07:15,950 --> 00:07:16,990
Grandma?

133
00:07:19,020 --> 00:07:20,160
Mom, you are a grandma.

134
00:07:20,560 --> 00:07:21,560
Hey, you little brat.

135
00:07:41,110 --> 00:07:43,410
This...

136
00:07:43,480 --> 00:07:45,780
If it has two lines, you're pregnant, right?

137
00:07:46,020 --> 00:07:47,980
Are you pregnant? You're pregnant?

138
00:07:50,420 --> 00:07:51,620
I'm going to be a dad!

139
00:07:51,620 --> 00:07:53,860
Mi Young, you've been through so much.

140
00:07:53,860 --> 00:07:55,830
The baby I had waited for so long,

141
00:07:57,830 --> 00:08:00,800
the baby I considered more precious than my own life,

142
00:08:03,630 --> 00:08:05,870
was suddenly taken from me one day.

143
00:08:10,110 --> 00:08:11,110
I...

144
00:08:12,940 --> 00:08:15,010
took medication that my husband gave me...

145
00:08:16,080 --> 00:08:17,310
and lost my baby.

146
00:08:19,150 --> 00:08:22,690
He gave me medication that I should have never taken.

147
00:08:24,650 --> 00:08:25,820
My husband...

148
00:08:27,020 --> 00:08:29,530
is a murderer who killed our baby.

149
00:08:42,740 --> 00:08:44,640
Are you sure you aren't mistaken?

150
00:08:45,040 --> 00:08:47,280
I already had the drug's components analysed.

151
00:08:47,840 --> 00:08:49,580
That medication was the direct cause...

152
00:08:50,210 --> 00:08:51,280
of my miscarriage.

153
00:08:55,150 --> 00:08:57,620
Still, how could pills cause a miscarriage?

154
00:08:58,020 --> 00:09:01,290
I'm sure those pills were meant to be good for you.

155
00:09:01,560 --> 00:09:04,330
That's right. Pill that were meant to be good for me.

156
00:09:05,160 --> 00:09:06,160
But...

157
00:09:07,160 --> 00:09:09,930
it was something a pregnant woman should never take.

158
00:09:14,400 --> 00:09:15,610
Wait.

159
00:09:16,640 --> 00:09:19,340
When did you start taking those pills?

160
00:09:20,080 --> 00:09:21,140
Let's see.

161
00:09:21,880 --> 00:09:26,550
Ji Won Ho gave me the pills around Chuseok,

162
00:09:27,620 --> 00:09:29,350
so I must have taken it for at least two months.

163
00:09:30,650 --> 00:09:31,690
Around Chuseok?

164
00:09:32,050 --> 00:09:33,890
We were sponsoring a group wedding then,

165
00:09:33,890 --> 00:09:35,830
so I was completely swamped.

166
00:09:36,260 --> 00:09:38,090
So even if I skipped meals,

167
00:09:38,090 --> 00:09:40,330
I made sure to take the pills without fail.

168
00:09:42,730 --> 00:09:44,100
Taking those pills...

169
00:09:45,970 --> 00:09:49,470
is the biggest regret of my life.

170
00:09:59,920 --> 00:10:00,920
What?

171
00:10:01,320 --> 00:10:02,450
What's with that look on your face?

172
00:10:03,250 --> 00:10:04,250
What?

173
00:10:05,250 --> 00:10:06,290
It's nothing.

174
00:10:10,360 --> 00:10:12,800
Anyway, you must have gone through so much.

175
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:15,000
To be honest,

176
00:10:15,830 --> 00:10:16,970
I'm still struggling.

177
00:10:19,200 --> 00:10:20,570
Even as time passes,

178
00:10:21,370 --> 00:10:22,940
I can't seem to forget.

179
00:10:26,896 --> 00:10:27,926
Gosh.

180
00:10:30,696 --> 00:10:32,866
Oh, my lawyer's here. I'm going to head up first.

181
00:10:32,936 --> 00:10:34,636
Okay. Hope it goes well.

182
00:10:34,896 --> 00:10:36,606
- Can you clean this up? - Of course.

183
00:10:36,606 --> 00:10:37,666
- Sorry. - It's okay.

184
00:10:42,180 --> 00:10:43,750
So that's what happened?

185
00:10:44,550 --> 00:10:45,620
But wait...

186
00:10:46,820 --> 00:10:48,960
Why didn't you tell me this before?

187
00:10:49,490 --> 00:10:51,890
- Pardon? - If it was something this serious,

188
00:10:52,090 --> 00:10:54,830
we wouldn't have had to be so roundabout.

189
00:10:56,670 --> 00:10:58,400
Are you sure it was your husband's mistake?

190
00:10:58,830 --> 00:11:00,900
If there's any evidence he gave you it intentionally...

191
00:11:00,970 --> 00:11:02,340
Absolutely not.

192
00:11:03,540 --> 00:11:04,770
My husband...

193
00:11:05,370 --> 00:11:08,280
wanted a child as desperately as I did.

194
00:11:09,550 --> 00:11:11,980
He had no reason to do something like that to me on purpose.

195
00:11:13,050 --> 00:11:14,780
But if that's the case,

196
00:11:15,920 --> 00:11:17,090
doesn't that make it even stranger?

197
00:11:19,090 --> 00:11:23,630
If your husband wanted to give you medication meant only for you,

198
00:11:24,390 --> 00:11:26,660
he would have simply asked for that when he bought it.

199
00:11:27,400 --> 00:11:28,400
That's true.

200
00:11:28,830 --> 00:11:30,300
When my husband bought the medication...

201
00:11:30,370 --> 00:11:33,470
He should have asked for medication for a pregnant woman.

202
00:11:34,470 --> 00:11:36,040
But what you took...

203
00:11:36,570 --> 00:11:39,380
was something fatal for pregnant women.

204
00:11:40,210 --> 00:11:43,580
I just thought my husband was being careless.

205
00:11:43,950 --> 00:11:45,810
During the delivery process,

206
00:11:46,880 --> 00:11:48,820
don't you think there could have been a mix-up?

207
00:11:49,220 --> 00:11:50,420
A mix-up?

208
00:11:56,790 --> 00:11:59,500
There's no way you'd give your wife pills like that.

209
00:12:00,700 --> 00:12:03,230
To win the lawsuit, don't you think she's going too far?

210
00:12:03,800 --> 00:12:05,000
But then again, Mi Young...

211
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:07,240
isn't the type to make something like that up.

212
00:12:10,840 --> 00:12:11,840
Wait a minute.

213
00:12:12,270 --> 00:12:14,040
Did you think of something?

214
00:12:16,710 --> 00:12:17,950
Could it be that?

215
00:12:20,120 --> 00:12:22,950
It'd be such a waste to send this back.

216
00:12:24,920 --> 00:12:26,790
If I were to buy this,

217
00:12:27,020 --> 00:12:29,290
it would easily cost several hundred dollars.

218
00:12:31,130 --> 00:12:32,860
What's so expensive?

219
00:12:34,030 --> 00:12:35,100
Oh, it's just...

220
00:12:35,800 --> 00:12:39,030
a holiday gift that came to the office for Chuseok.

221
00:12:39,600 --> 00:12:42,610
CEO Baek told me to return any gifts...

222
00:12:42,710 --> 00:12:44,970
that might be considered a bribe without a second thought.

223
00:12:45,510 --> 00:12:46,810
Then just send it back.

224
00:12:46,980 --> 00:12:48,710
What if something goes wrong because you accepted it?

225
00:12:49,110 --> 00:12:51,980
But with this one, it's a little unclear...

226
00:12:52,050 --> 00:12:54,350
if it's a bribe or not.

227
00:12:54,480 --> 00:12:55,680
Where's it from?

228
00:12:57,020 --> 00:13:00,720
Well, from some place with a lot of money.

229
00:13:01,190 --> 00:13:02,990
A wealthy company that's so rich...

230
00:13:03,060 --> 00:13:05,490
that they wouldn't even notice giving away something like this.

231
00:13:06,400 --> 00:13:07,400
Is that so?

232
00:13:07,830 --> 00:13:08,830
Look,

233
00:13:09,060 --> 00:13:12,640
CEO Ji, from the looks of it, these are very expensive pills.

234
00:13:13,200 --> 00:13:15,740
Just one pill will give you a huge boost of energy.

235
00:13:16,270 --> 00:13:17,440
A huge boost of energy?

236
00:13:17,640 --> 00:13:18,640
Yes.

237
00:13:21,140 --> 00:13:22,480
Should we...

238
00:13:23,080 --> 00:13:24,380
give this to Mi Young?

239
00:13:25,080 --> 00:13:26,120
Mi Young?

240
00:13:26,120 --> 00:13:29,490
She's had morning sickness lately and hasn't been able to eat well.

241
00:13:29,550 --> 00:13:31,590
It would be good for her to take something like this.

242
00:13:33,060 --> 00:13:35,460
Mi Young will be angry if she finds out.

243
00:13:36,660 --> 00:13:38,130
That's why...

244
00:13:38,560 --> 00:13:40,830
you shouldn't say it's from a client.

245
00:13:41,400 --> 00:13:43,800
Just say you bought it.

246
00:13:44,500 --> 00:13:47,200
- What do you think? - You gave that to Mi Young?

247
00:13:47,940 --> 00:13:49,240
Yes.

248
00:13:49,410 --> 00:13:51,170
I gave it to her as if I bought it.

249
00:13:51,410 --> 00:13:53,380
Did you even check what kind of pills they were?

250
00:13:54,540 --> 00:13:57,280
I just heard A Ri say it was expensive and good.

251
00:13:57,410 --> 00:13:58,680
But she was pregnant.

252
00:13:58,750 --> 00:14:01,080
You should have checked the ingredients carefully.

253
00:14:01,680 --> 00:14:04,290
Or you should have just been honest and told her it was a gift.

254
00:14:04,890 --> 00:14:06,660
Why did you pretend you bought it?

255
00:14:06,860 --> 00:14:09,460
You know how it is. When women are pregnant,

256
00:14:09,530 --> 00:14:10,860
they want their husbands to be attentive...

257
00:14:10,930 --> 00:14:12,560
and show they care.

258
00:14:12,830 --> 00:14:14,100
I just thought if I said I bought it,

259
00:14:14,160 --> 00:14:15,700
she'd be happier.

260
00:14:16,130 --> 00:14:17,530
You tried to take credit for something free,

261
00:14:17,800 --> 00:14:19,030
and look what happened.

262
00:14:19,470 --> 00:14:21,670
But I'm sure it's not that kind of pill.

263
00:14:23,810 --> 00:14:26,280
I shouldn't be sitting here. I should just go ask A Ri.

264
00:14:26,280 --> 00:14:27,410
Hey, wait a minute.

265
00:14:30,210 --> 00:14:32,350
If it really is because of the pills from Director Song,

266
00:14:32,920 --> 00:14:33,980
what will happen?

267
00:14:34,450 --> 00:14:35,480
What?

268
00:14:35,480 --> 00:14:38,350
If she finds out her best friend had a miscarriage because of her,

269
00:14:39,590 --> 00:14:40,590
do you think...

270
00:14:41,260 --> 00:14:42,320
Director Song will be okay?

271
00:14:43,690 --> 00:14:45,560
Of course she won't.

272
00:14:46,360 --> 00:14:48,560
I know it's not my place to get involved in your marriage,

273
00:14:49,770 --> 00:14:51,470
but you really need to think this through.

274
00:14:52,200 --> 00:14:53,970
I'm talking about this constant emotional fighting,

275
00:14:54,270 --> 00:14:56,110
always bringing up the past.

276
00:14:57,440 --> 00:14:59,210
What happened with the baby is truly tragic,

277
00:14:59,610 --> 00:15:03,410
but losing Director Song over this doesn't seem right.

278
00:15:04,450 --> 00:15:06,010
Still, I have to check.

279
00:15:06,080 --> 00:15:08,280
It might turn out to have nothing to do with A Ri.

280
00:15:08,380 --> 00:15:09,390
Given the circumstances,

281
00:15:09,450 --> 00:15:11,020
it's obvious it was Director Song's mistake.

282
00:15:11,090 --> 00:15:13,690
Okay. I understand what you're saying.

283
00:15:14,220 --> 00:15:16,130
I'll find the right time to bring this up with her.

284
00:15:16,330 --> 00:15:17,730
I'll try not to shock A Ri too much.

285
00:15:24,800 --> 00:15:26,900
(Calvin Care Holdings, Nutritional Facts And Directions)

286
00:15:31,570 --> 00:15:32,880
(Supplements Unsafe for Pregnant Women)

287
00:15:36,850 --> 00:15:37,850
Director Song.

288
00:15:39,350 --> 00:15:40,450
Yes, Vice President Kang.

289
00:15:40,920 --> 00:15:41,920
Are you okay?

290
00:15:42,220 --> 00:15:43,220
Yes?

291
00:15:44,290 --> 00:15:45,320
What about?

292
00:15:46,460 --> 00:15:47,460
It's nothing.

293
00:15:48,290 --> 00:15:50,430
By the way, did you place the fabric order?

294
00:15:51,230 --> 00:15:52,460
Oh, right.

295
00:15:53,060 --> 00:15:54,830
I was supposed to place the order today.

296
00:15:55,460 --> 00:15:57,830
I'm sorry. I forgot.

297
00:15:59,070 --> 00:16:00,540
Please have it done this morning.

298
00:16:01,270 --> 00:16:03,070
Yes, I'll place the order right away.

299
00:16:21,620 --> 00:16:23,790
(Jihwaja Motel)

300
00:16:26,700 --> 00:16:28,830
I can't just kick that troublemaker out.

301
00:16:29,200 --> 00:16:30,230
What am I going to do?

302
00:16:30,600 --> 00:16:32,870
Couldn't we just ignore her for now?

303
00:16:33,100 --> 00:16:35,240
But if we do that, who knows what trouble she'll stir up.

304
00:16:35,840 --> 00:16:36,840
That's true.

305
00:16:37,540 --> 00:16:39,110
The thought alone is terrifying.

306
00:16:40,180 --> 00:16:43,410
Mom, what if we start some smoke in front of her room?

307
00:16:43,650 --> 00:16:44,650
What?

308
00:16:44,710 --> 00:16:46,950
If she thinks there's a fire, she'll come running out, right?

309
00:16:47,080 --> 00:16:48,580
Are you trying to burn the house down...

310
00:16:48,580 --> 00:16:49,650
to get rid of a mouse?

311
00:16:51,720 --> 00:16:54,220
But that girl looks so normal.

312
00:16:54,320 --> 00:16:55,720
I don't get what she sees in Won Ho.

313
00:16:55,820 --> 00:16:57,130
What's not to like?

314
00:16:57,290 --> 00:17:01,260
Won Ho is handsome and capable. He's second to none.

315
00:17:01,560 --> 00:17:02,970
Even after he breaks up with that fox,

316
00:17:03,030 --> 00:17:04,900
he could get remarried two more times.

317
00:17:05,170 --> 00:17:07,070
Still, two more times is a bit...

318
00:17:09,140 --> 00:17:10,140
Mom.

319
00:17:10,510 --> 00:17:12,770
- That's it. - What?

320
00:17:13,010 --> 00:17:14,940
You're not the first.

321
00:17:15,340 --> 00:17:17,110
The one before you was in Room 203.

322
00:17:17,750 --> 00:17:19,550
The one before her was in Room 403.

323
00:17:19,750 --> 00:17:22,520
Plenty have already come and gone. Women who liked Won Ho.

324
00:17:22,850 --> 00:17:24,750
To him, you're just one of those women,

325
00:17:24,750 --> 00:17:25,850
one who is just passing through.

326
00:17:26,420 --> 00:17:28,290
The only woman who will be with Won Ho until the end...

327
00:17:28,460 --> 00:17:29,760
is my sister-in-law.

328
00:17:35,130 --> 00:17:36,400
Was what I said that funny?

329
00:17:38,370 --> 00:17:40,940
No. It's just so ridiculous.

330
00:17:41,740 --> 00:17:43,840
- What? - It is ridiculous.

331
00:17:44,170 --> 00:17:47,540
Making up a story like that just to get rid of me.

332
00:17:47,640 --> 00:17:49,380
I'm telling you, it's the truth.

333
00:17:49,680 --> 00:17:51,180
Don't waste your breath.

334
00:17:51,610 --> 00:17:53,520
I don't care if a truckload of women have come and gone.

335
00:17:53,680 --> 00:17:55,350
There's no way I'm leaving.

336
00:17:55,650 --> 00:17:57,190
What do you like so much about Won Ho?

337
00:17:57,950 --> 00:17:58,950
It's just...

338
00:17:59,790 --> 00:18:00,860
destiny.

339
00:18:00,920 --> 00:18:02,990
- What? - I knew the moment I saw him...

340
00:18:03,290 --> 00:18:06,730
that CEO Ji is the man of my destiny.

341
00:18:06,930 --> 00:18:09,500
That's enough. If you keep this up...

342
00:18:09,570 --> 00:18:11,870
You're the one who needs to stop.

343
00:18:12,130 --> 00:18:13,440
When I lose my temper,

344
00:18:14,540 --> 00:18:15,770
I get really nasty.

345
00:18:16,310 --> 00:18:18,340
So what if you get nasty?

346
00:18:18,910 --> 00:18:20,580
Are you going to hurt me or something?

347
00:18:22,410 --> 00:18:23,410
That's right.

348
00:18:24,250 --> 00:18:26,720
I should take care of that guy first.

349
00:18:31,190 --> 00:18:32,990
Yes, is this the customer service center...

350
00:18:32,990 --> 00:18:34,920
for the pharmaceutical company?

351
00:18:35,790 --> 00:18:38,990
I'm calling because I have a question about a supplement.

352
00:18:39,730 --> 00:18:40,730
Yes.

353
00:18:41,530 --> 00:18:44,200
The specific supplement is...

354
00:18:44,970 --> 00:18:46,100
Director Song.

355
00:18:47,040 --> 00:18:49,040
Yes, I'll have to call you back.

356
00:18:50,470 --> 00:18:52,940
Oh, Young Yun, what is it?

357
00:18:53,110 --> 00:18:54,140
Director Song,

358
00:18:54,340 --> 00:18:56,710
you should get to the office right away.

359
00:18:57,710 --> 00:18:59,250
How could you make such a huge mistake?

360
00:18:59,680 --> 00:19:02,350
How could you accidentally add an extra zero?

361
00:19:02,850 --> 00:19:04,620
It's a good thing I checked.

362
00:19:04,850 --> 00:19:06,390
What would have happened if the order had gone through...

363
00:19:06,390 --> 00:19:07,390
like that?

364
00:19:08,160 --> 00:19:09,190
I'm so sorry.

365
00:19:09,520 --> 00:19:10,560
I'm so sorry.

366
00:19:10,790 --> 00:19:14,160
Director Song. Where on earth is your head at?

367
00:19:16,970 --> 00:19:17,970
Vice President Kang.

368
00:19:18,800 --> 00:19:20,400
Let's leave it at that.

369
00:19:21,270 --> 00:19:23,510
Besides, it's been handled, thankfully.

370
00:19:29,750 --> 00:19:30,880
Also,

371
00:19:31,750 --> 00:19:32,780
I think Director Song...

372
00:19:33,420 --> 00:19:36,250
- knows it was her mistake. - What?

373
00:19:36,450 --> 00:19:39,520
- A Ri knows already? How? - Mi Young must have told her.

374
00:19:40,290 --> 00:19:42,860
I saw a search history for supplements...

375
00:19:44,230 --> 00:19:46,460
on Director Song's computer earlier.

376
00:19:48,330 --> 00:19:50,900
Supplements that pregnant women shouldn't take.

377
00:20:12,920 --> 00:20:14,620
Hey. What's going on?

378
00:20:15,920 --> 00:20:18,490
Oh, that place? Yes, I like it too.

379
00:20:19,860 --> 00:20:20,860
Should we?

380
00:20:21,460 --> 00:20:22,460
What time?

381
00:20:24,570 --> 00:20:26,170
Okay, sounds good.

382
00:20:27,000 --> 00:20:29,070
The reservation is under Calvin, right?

383
00:20:30,670 --> 00:20:32,070
Okay, see you later.

384
00:20:35,110 --> 00:20:36,450
You scared me.

385
00:20:37,310 --> 00:20:39,080
Gosh, you came in so quietly.

386
00:20:39,150 --> 00:20:40,520
Why are you so surprised?

387
00:20:40,720 --> 00:20:42,480
Do I have to kick the door in for you to hear me?

388
00:20:42,880 --> 00:20:44,590
What, do you have something to say?

389
00:20:44,990 --> 00:20:47,020
You seem to be pretty close with Calvin these days.

390
00:20:47,720 --> 00:20:50,790
- What? - Looks like you're off somewhere.

391
00:20:50,860 --> 00:20:52,030
What's it to you?

392
00:20:52,530 --> 00:20:55,030
Says one half of the inseparable Couple of the Century.

393
00:20:56,160 --> 00:20:57,200
"Couple of the Century?"

394
00:20:57,700 --> 00:20:58,970
Hey, I need to get back to work.

395
00:20:59,030 --> 00:21:00,270
If you have something to say, say it and leave.

396
00:21:03,370 --> 00:21:04,710
If something...

397
00:21:06,240 --> 00:21:08,080
really went wrong because of those pills,

398
00:21:10,350 --> 00:21:12,010
could you forgive the person who gave it to you?

399
00:21:13,050 --> 00:21:14,050
What?

400
00:21:14,050 --> 00:21:17,050
I'm saying, if it wasn't me but someone else,

401
00:21:18,390 --> 00:21:19,920
could you forgive that person?

402
00:21:21,790 --> 00:21:22,790
First of all,

403
00:21:24,660 --> 00:21:25,860
I took that supplement,

404
00:21:27,030 --> 00:21:28,360
and something happened to our baby.

405
00:21:29,600 --> 00:21:31,000
That is an unchangeable fact.

406
00:21:32,330 --> 00:21:33,340
And...

407
00:21:34,470 --> 00:21:36,100
would I be able to forgive the person...

408
00:21:36,510 --> 00:21:38,570
who gave me the wrong pills if it wasn't you?

409
00:21:40,840 --> 00:21:41,840
No.

410
00:21:43,810 --> 00:21:45,650
The only reason I put up with it was because it was you.

411
00:21:47,880 --> 00:21:50,550
The only way I could endure it for three years...

412
00:21:53,620 --> 00:21:56,830
was because the person who gave me that supplement wasn't a stranger.

413
00:21:58,960 --> 00:22:00,730
It was because it was you.

414
00:22:10,470 --> 00:22:12,470
(Conference Room)

415
00:22:23,120 --> 00:22:24,120
I...

416
00:22:26,290 --> 00:22:27,920
took medication that my husband gave me...

417
00:22:29,360 --> 00:22:30,690
and lost my baby.

418
00:22:41,040 --> 00:22:44,140
CEO Ji, I have something urgent to tell you.

419
00:22:44,640 --> 00:22:46,640
I'll be waiting at the cafe up ahead.

420
00:22:53,380 --> 00:22:54,380
CEO Ji.

421
00:22:56,250 --> 00:22:59,750
The reason I asked to see you out here is...

422
00:22:59,890 --> 00:23:02,220
Well, I mean, it's not that...

423
00:23:04,360 --> 00:23:06,260
You heard from Mi Young, right?

424
00:23:09,330 --> 00:23:10,400
About the pills...

425
00:23:11,300 --> 00:23:12,300
Yes.

426
00:23:12,970 --> 00:23:14,040
I heard.

427
00:23:20,010 --> 00:23:23,210
Still, thank you. I wasn't sure how to bring it up,

428
00:23:23,580 --> 00:23:24,810
so I was really hesitant.

429
00:23:26,110 --> 00:23:27,820
So thank you for being brave enough to do it first.

430
00:23:28,050 --> 00:23:29,480
But I really...

431
00:23:30,290 --> 00:23:32,350
didn't think it would be a problem.

432
00:23:34,520 --> 00:23:35,960
I know.

433
00:23:38,860 --> 00:23:40,100
You're not a pharmacist, A Ri.

434
00:23:40,160 --> 00:23:42,560
How could you possibly know all of the ingredients?

435
00:23:43,600 --> 00:23:44,600
It was just...

436
00:23:45,900 --> 00:23:47,370
really bad luck.

437
00:23:48,370 --> 00:23:51,770
Unfortunately, those pills were very harmful to pregnant women.

438
00:23:53,480 --> 00:23:54,840
That's not it.

439
00:23:56,850 --> 00:23:57,910
It's not?

440
00:23:58,280 --> 00:24:02,480
It was just a simple health supplement.

441
00:24:02,680 --> 00:24:04,850
It was packed with all sorts of healthy ingredients.

442
00:24:05,490 --> 00:24:08,560
I called the pharmaceutical company earlier and confirmed everything.

443
00:24:08,760 --> 00:24:09,890
Oh, really?

444
00:24:11,430 --> 00:24:13,560
Right. I knew it.

445
00:24:13,630 --> 00:24:16,530
No wonder. That didn't make any sense.

446
00:24:18,830 --> 00:24:21,440
Oh, A Ri, I'm sorry. I guess I jumped to conclusions.

447
00:24:21,500 --> 00:24:23,470
I'm so sorry. I mean...

448
00:24:23,810 --> 00:24:24,910
Oh, thank you.

449
00:24:26,740 --> 00:24:28,380
No...

450
00:24:29,640 --> 00:24:31,050
It's my fault.

451
00:24:32,810 --> 00:24:34,080
How is it your fault, A Ri?

452
00:24:34,150 --> 00:24:36,150
You said there was nothing wrong with the pills, right?

453
00:24:36,220 --> 00:24:38,820
There's nothing wrong with those pills.

454
00:24:39,920 --> 00:24:42,360
But the person who gave them to me...

455
00:24:44,960 --> 00:24:46,630
was Calvin.

456
00:24:48,060 --> 00:24:49,060
What?

457
00:24:49,400 --> 00:24:50,670
Back then,

458
00:24:51,870 --> 00:24:53,540
the person who sent the pills...

459
00:24:54,270 --> 00:24:56,000
was Calvin.

460
00:25:08,220 --> 00:25:10,020
When I checked the package,

461
00:25:10,190 --> 00:25:12,750
the sender was Calvin.

462
00:25:13,250 --> 00:25:15,760
I knew Mi Young would be furious if she found out,

463
00:25:16,020 --> 00:25:18,390
but since Calvin was the one who sent it,

464
00:25:18,490 --> 00:25:19,890
I just assumed it had to be something good.

465
00:25:19,960 --> 00:25:22,400
That's what I thought. That's why, but...

466
00:25:23,630 --> 00:25:24,700
If...

467
00:25:25,970 --> 00:25:27,440
Calvin...

468
00:25:28,540 --> 00:25:31,410
tampered with those pills somehow...

469
00:25:35,380 --> 00:25:36,540
Three years ago,

470
00:25:37,480 --> 00:25:41,280
the day the detailed test results came back negative for paternity,

471
00:25:41,850 --> 00:25:44,220
I happened to see Mi Young at the hospital.

472
00:25:45,750 --> 00:25:47,990
She looked pregnant.

473
00:25:51,490 --> 00:25:53,600
I couldn't bring myself to say hello,

474
00:25:53,960 --> 00:25:55,860
and just watched her from a distance.

475
00:25:57,030 --> 00:25:58,830
Seeing Mi Young pregnant...

476
00:25:59,670 --> 00:26:01,200
gave me a strange feeling.

477
00:26:03,870 --> 00:26:05,610
It was a bitter feeling.

478
00:26:20,990 --> 00:26:22,090
I thought we...

479
00:26:22,520 --> 00:26:24,390
were done with each other.

480
00:26:24,790 --> 00:26:26,690
We might have been.

481
00:26:27,260 --> 00:26:29,260
If you hadn't done what you did to me.

482
00:26:29,960 --> 00:26:31,030
What I did?

483
00:26:31,130 --> 00:26:32,530
You ordered it, didn't you?

484
00:26:33,200 --> 00:26:34,540
Having me pushed off the cliff.

485
00:26:34,900 --> 00:26:38,010
Are you still angry about being pushed off a cliff?

486
00:26:38,610 --> 00:26:41,780
- What? - You fell off a cliff,

487
00:26:41,880 --> 00:26:43,580
and you're completely fine.

488
00:26:44,350 --> 00:26:46,050
If I were you, I'd be grateful.

489
00:26:48,520 --> 00:26:50,850
Like I'd been given a new lease on life.

490
00:26:51,250 --> 00:26:52,850
Maybe I'd want to live differently than before...

491
00:26:53,190 --> 00:26:55,460
and be a better person.

492
00:26:57,390 --> 00:26:58,690
Are you messing with me?

493
00:27:00,460 --> 00:27:02,030
I will get my revenge.

494
00:27:03,130 --> 00:27:06,840
What you did to me, I'm going to do the same to you.

495
00:27:11,010 --> 00:27:12,010
Go on.

496
00:27:12,310 --> 00:27:13,580
You're welcome to try anytime.

497
00:27:14,480 --> 00:27:15,880
But before you do,

498
00:27:16,240 --> 00:27:17,480
bring me proof.

499
00:27:18,110 --> 00:27:19,110
What?

500
00:27:19,180 --> 00:27:21,580
Proof that I pushed you off the cliff.

501
00:27:22,750 --> 00:27:24,250
Whether it's revenge or something else,

502
00:27:24,550 --> 00:27:26,960
shouldn't you get your facts straight first?

503
00:27:35,330 --> 00:27:38,170
- Yes. - Sir, you have a visitor.

504
00:27:38,400 --> 00:27:40,540
- Where is Calvin right now? - You can't go in right now.

505
00:27:40,600 --> 00:27:43,200
- Is he here? I just need a minute. - Please wait, sir.

506
00:27:44,240 --> 00:27:45,370
CEO Ji.

507
00:27:46,510 --> 00:27:48,040
What brings you here so suddenly at this hour?

508
00:27:48,140 --> 00:27:50,480
Something just came up that I need to ask you.

509
00:27:50,750 --> 00:27:52,550
You're here to confront something too?

510
00:27:52,550 --> 00:27:53,920
Stay out of this.

511
00:27:56,950 --> 00:27:58,420
I said, get out.

512
00:27:59,490 --> 00:28:00,490
Okay.

513
00:28:09,430 --> 00:28:11,670
(Hotel Calvin)

514
00:28:12,430 --> 00:28:15,170
What is it you want to know? Go ahead and ask.

515
00:28:15,570 --> 00:28:16,740
Do you remember...

516
00:28:17,570 --> 00:28:19,770
the supplement you sent to Mi Young three years ago?

517
00:28:20,070 --> 00:28:23,580
Are you referring to the holiday gift our company sends...

518
00:28:24,310 --> 00:28:25,610
to our business partners?

519
00:28:25,980 --> 00:28:27,150
Yes, that's it.

520
00:28:27,550 --> 00:28:30,320
That health supplement you sent under your name.

521
00:28:30,590 --> 00:28:31,690
Yes, I remember.

522
00:28:31,820 --> 00:28:32,820
Was it a coincidence?

523
00:28:33,220 --> 00:28:35,120
- What? - Are you telling me...

524
00:28:35,120 --> 00:28:37,360
that when you found out your son wasn't biologically yours,

525
00:28:37,830 --> 00:28:40,130
and happened to run into a pregnant Mi Young,

526
00:28:40,200 --> 00:28:41,800
you sent her that supplement...

527
00:28:42,160 --> 00:28:43,400
purely by coincidence?

528
00:28:44,300 --> 00:28:46,200
I'm sorry, what are you trying to say?

529
00:28:46,300 --> 00:28:48,300
She lost the baby because of that supplement.

530
00:28:48,840 --> 00:28:50,210
Lost the baby?

531
00:28:50,270 --> 00:28:52,110
At least, that's what Mi Young believes.

532
00:28:52,440 --> 00:28:54,540
That she miscarried after taking it.

533
00:28:54,610 --> 00:28:56,580
So she's been suspecting me as the one who gave it to her,

534
00:28:56,640 --> 00:28:58,310
and blaming me all this time.

535
00:28:58,380 --> 00:28:59,850
No, that can't be.

536
00:29:00,880 --> 00:29:03,480
That supplement was just a common something anyone can take...

537
00:29:03,550 --> 00:29:05,950
Sure, the supplement itself was probably harmless.

538
00:29:06,650 --> 00:29:08,890
Unless someone tampered with it.

539
00:29:10,460 --> 00:29:11,590
Tampered with it?

540
00:29:11,730 --> 00:29:12,860
Yes.

541
00:29:13,030 --> 00:29:16,200
- Tampered with it. - So you're saying, Ji Won Ho,

542
00:29:16,560 --> 00:29:18,830
that in order to harm Mi Young's baby,

543
00:29:18,900 --> 00:29:22,200
I deliberately tampered with the supplement.

544
00:29:22,940 --> 00:29:24,210
Is that what you're trying to say?

545
00:29:24,210 --> 00:29:25,210
Other than that possibility,

546
00:29:25,210 --> 00:29:27,580
I can't see any other way to explain this.

547
00:29:30,910 --> 00:29:31,980
If so,

548
00:29:32,480 --> 00:29:34,380
does that make you feel better?

549
00:29:35,080 --> 00:29:36,080
What?

550
00:29:36,150 --> 00:29:37,750
If Mi Young miscarried because she took...

551
00:29:37,820 --> 00:29:39,420
the supplement I happened to give her,

552
00:29:39,620 --> 00:29:40,920
and if the fact that she lost her child...

553
00:29:40,920 --> 00:29:42,860
and has a wound that will never heal...

554
00:29:42,960 --> 00:29:44,160
is all my fault,

555
00:29:44,390 --> 00:29:47,700
I'm asking if that would make you feel much better.

556
00:29:47,760 --> 00:29:48,760
Stop talking nonsense.

557
00:29:48,830 --> 00:29:51,830
- Just answer my question. - I think you should leave now.

558
00:29:52,470 --> 00:29:54,500
Any more conversation would be a waste of time.

559
00:29:56,800 --> 00:29:58,270
You tampered with it, didn't you?

560
00:30:02,410 --> 00:30:03,510
If Mi Young didn't have a child,

561
00:30:03,580 --> 00:30:05,450
it would be easier for you to get her back after the divorce,

562
00:30:05,510 --> 00:30:06,910
wouldn't it?

563
00:30:07,120 --> 00:30:09,520
You're the one who did it, you bastard.

564
00:30:09,580 --> 00:30:10,690
Am I wrong?

565
00:30:12,590 --> 00:30:13,590
Hey, you.

566
00:30:14,190 --> 00:30:15,320
Get your hands off me.

567
00:30:15,660 --> 00:30:16,860
Why do you think...

568
00:30:17,230 --> 00:30:20,230
I just stood by and watched Mi Young marry a scumbag like you?

569
00:30:20,830 --> 00:30:22,800
Because Mi Young chose you.

570
00:30:23,330 --> 00:30:26,000
Because you were the one Mi Young wanted.

571
00:30:26,800 --> 00:30:27,970
Listen to me.

572
00:30:28,740 --> 00:30:31,870
I would die for Mi Young.

573
00:30:32,170 --> 00:30:34,880
Unlike you, who'd shamelessly cheat on her.

574
00:30:35,010 --> 00:30:36,780
I'm nothing like you.

575
00:30:40,480 --> 00:30:41,620
Darn it.

576
00:30:51,560 --> 00:30:54,360
Ouch, that hurts. Gosh, that hurts.

577
00:30:55,430 --> 00:30:56,930
He could've just used his words.

578
00:30:57,000 --> 00:30:58,730
What is he, a gangster or something?

579
00:30:59,400 --> 00:31:01,040
And he's freakishly strong.

580
00:31:03,300 --> 00:31:04,610
Are you okay?

581
00:31:07,940 --> 00:31:10,350
What? You haven't left yet?

582
00:31:15,220 --> 00:31:17,720
But didn't you say Calvin fired you?

583
00:31:18,390 --> 00:31:19,390
I was.

584
00:31:19,720 --> 00:31:21,720
That's why you helped me out.

585
00:31:22,320 --> 00:31:23,930
What are you doing here anyway?

586
00:31:23,990 --> 00:31:25,160
Is there something you need?

587
00:31:25,460 --> 00:31:27,130
I'm here to investigate the case.

588
00:31:27,200 --> 00:31:30,530
Calvin is my prime murder suspect.

589
00:31:31,100 --> 00:31:32,100
What?

590
00:31:32,370 --> 00:31:34,600
When I was pushed off the cliff the other day,

591
00:31:35,000 --> 00:31:36,300
Calvin was...

592
00:31:36,840 --> 00:31:38,340
behind it.

593
00:31:39,410 --> 00:31:40,940
No way.

594
00:31:41,010 --> 00:31:44,450
It's true. You just saw for yourself, CEO Ji.

595
00:31:44,780 --> 00:31:47,380
He grabs you by the collar just for saying a few words.

596
00:31:47,880 --> 00:31:49,950
Getting rid of someone...

597
00:31:50,120 --> 00:31:51,550
would be nothing to a guy like him.

598
00:31:51,720 --> 00:31:52,750
That's true.

599
00:31:52,990 --> 00:31:54,990
That guy has serious anger management issues.

600
00:31:55,060 --> 00:31:57,390
I'm serious, I almost suffocated just now.

601
00:31:57,630 --> 00:32:00,830
That prank must have been Calvin's doing too.

602
00:32:01,130 --> 00:32:02,130
Wait a minute...

603
00:32:02,260 --> 00:32:04,570
Were you outside listening to all of that?

604
00:32:04,670 --> 00:32:06,400
I wasn't trying to listen,

605
00:32:06,870 --> 00:32:08,940
but I couldn't help hearing it.

606
00:32:10,670 --> 00:32:13,170
But seeing him get so fired up like that...

607
00:32:13,410 --> 00:32:14,980
makes me think it might not be him.

608
00:32:15,240 --> 00:32:17,010
This is so confusing.

609
00:32:17,080 --> 00:32:18,380
There's nothing to be confused about.

610
00:32:19,010 --> 00:32:20,280
Without a doubt,

611
00:32:20,350 --> 00:32:21,780
Calvin is the culprit.

612
00:32:23,920 --> 00:32:27,190
When you're this stressed out, you have to eat to feel better.

613
00:32:27,820 --> 00:32:29,260
Let's go get something good to eat.

614
00:32:30,430 --> 00:32:31,530
I can't.

615
00:32:31,990 --> 00:32:32,990
Why not?

616
00:32:33,060 --> 00:32:35,830
I said I can't. Not until I clear my name.

617
00:32:36,060 --> 00:32:39,630
- Clear your name? - My wife thinks I'm a murderer.

618
00:32:39,800 --> 00:32:41,370
Until I catch the real culprit behind the miscarriage...

619
00:32:41,440 --> 00:32:43,340
and clear my name,

620
00:32:43,740 --> 00:32:46,440
- let's not see each other. - Why?

621
00:32:46,710 --> 00:32:48,410
What does you being falsely accused...

622
00:32:48,480 --> 00:32:50,610
have to do with us seeing each other?

623
00:32:50,680 --> 00:32:53,610
It has everything to do with it. This is all your fault.

624
00:32:53,980 --> 00:32:55,850
My wife blew up because of you,

625
00:32:55,920 --> 00:32:57,450
and that's how this mess started.

626
00:32:57,450 --> 00:32:58,790
What do you mean?

627
00:32:58,890 --> 00:33:00,820
Anyway, I'm leaving.

628
00:33:02,590 --> 00:33:04,590
Hey, wait up.

629
00:33:11,800 --> 00:33:13,200
Hey. CEO Ji.

630
00:33:14,470 --> 00:33:17,070
Hey, seriously.

631
00:33:28,620 --> 00:33:31,490
Please give it some more thought.

632
00:33:31,520 --> 00:33:33,450
It will look even more spectacular under the lights.

633
00:33:33,620 --> 00:33:35,390
So please take that into consideration.

634
00:33:35,520 --> 00:33:37,260
Think it over...

635
00:33:39,790 --> 00:33:42,060
You have hands, and you have feet...

636
00:33:42,500 --> 00:33:45,570
My dear Dallae, when did you grow so much?

637
00:33:46,830 --> 00:33:48,500
Just hang in there a little longer.

638
00:33:48,900 --> 00:33:52,370
When you're born, Mommy will take even better care of you.

639
00:33:55,880 --> 00:33:58,250
- CEO Baek. - Oh, yes. Come in.

640
00:33:58,380 --> 00:34:00,410
(CEO's Office)

641
00:34:01,020 --> 00:34:03,250
I hope I'm not interrupting.

642
00:34:03,920 --> 00:34:04,950
Not at all.

643
00:34:05,550 --> 00:34:07,090
What can I do for you?

644
00:34:07,620 --> 00:34:09,060
Oh, well...

645
00:34:14,630 --> 00:34:16,960
What is this?

646
00:34:25,370 --> 00:34:26,440
Goodbye.

647
00:34:28,780 --> 00:34:29,780
CEO Baek.

648
00:34:30,980 --> 00:34:32,310
It was a massive success.

649
00:34:32,550 --> 00:34:34,080
All the clients who had fittings today...

650
00:34:34,150 --> 00:34:35,920
loved their dresses so much...

651
00:34:35,980 --> 00:34:37,250
that they booked with us on the spot.

652
00:34:37,920 --> 00:34:41,720
Even a client who'd been shopping around for a while...

653
00:34:41,790 --> 00:34:43,760
booked with us the minute she walked in today.

654
00:34:43,990 --> 00:34:46,060
Really? That's wonderful.

655
00:34:46,290 --> 00:34:49,400
It really reminds me how incredible CEO Ji is.

656
00:34:49,560 --> 00:34:52,600
I mean, it doesn't seem like he does much,

657
00:34:53,000 --> 00:34:56,100
but he still manages to create these perfect dresses every season.

658
00:34:56,670 --> 00:34:57,810
Don't you agree, CEO Baek?

659
00:34:58,710 --> 00:34:59,710
Yes.

660
00:35:01,240 --> 00:35:04,310
By the way, Vice President Kang...

661
00:35:05,450 --> 00:35:09,180
There's something I'd like to ask you...

662
00:35:10,220 --> 00:35:11,220
What is it?

663
00:35:12,720 --> 00:35:13,750
Well...

664
00:35:16,290 --> 00:35:17,460
Just a moment.

665
00:35:19,890 --> 00:35:21,000
Hello?

666
00:35:23,300 --> 00:35:24,330
Welcome.

667
00:35:37,580 --> 00:35:39,310
Ji Won Ho...

668
00:35:39,880 --> 00:35:41,480
came to see me today.

669
00:35:41,880 --> 00:35:42,980
Won Ho did?

670
00:35:44,190 --> 00:35:46,420
Why? What was it about?

671
00:35:46,850 --> 00:35:48,320
He asked about the supplements...

672
00:35:48,790 --> 00:35:51,460
I sent to your company about three years ago.

673
00:35:52,130 --> 00:35:53,130
Supplements?

674
00:35:53,190 --> 00:35:54,560
The one I sent three years ago during the holidays,

675
00:35:54,560 --> 00:35:56,760
under the Calvin Hotel name.

676
00:35:57,160 --> 00:35:58,170
Don't you remember?

677
00:35:59,000 --> 00:36:01,340
It was a health supplement in a purple container.

678
00:36:01,770 --> 00:36:03,070
Could it be...

679
00:36:03,370 --> 00:36:06,340
similar to that supplement you gave me before?

680
00:36:06,610 --> 00:36:07,680
Yes, that's the one.

681
00:36:09,410 --> 00:36:10,710
Take this when you feel tired.

682
00:36:11,510 --> 00:36:12,510
Thanks.

683
00:36:19,750 --> 00:36:21,120
(Energy Care Up)

684
00:36:23,160 --> 00:36:24,230
Because of those pills...

685
00:36:25,090 --> 00:36:26,130
That's impossible.

686
00:36:28,800 --> 00:36:31,000
I never even opened the box.

687
00:36:32,700 --> 00:36:33,700
So of course,

688
00:36:35,270 --> 00:36:36,300
I never took it.

689
00:36:40,370 --> 00:36:42,640
- Really? - That supplement...

690
00:36:43,610 --> 00:36:46,050
was made by a company affiliated with Calvin.

691
00:36:47,280 --> 00:36:50,350
Back then, I felt too resentful toward you.

692
00:36:52,690 --> 00:36:53,690
I'm sorry.

693
00:37:01,560 --> 00:37:02,600
What's wrong?

694
00:37:03,660 --> 00:37:04,670
I'm sorry, Mi Young.

695
00:37:06,400 --> 00:37:07,570
I'm so sorry.

696
00:37:09,300 --> 00:37:11,110
When I found out you were pregnant,

697
00:37:12,210 --> 00:37:14,140
I didn't want you to have a healthy baby.

698
00:37:16,440 --> 00:37:17,510
That child...

699
00:37:18,910 --> 00:37:20,410
could have been my child.

700
00:37:23,150 --> 00:37:24,420
To be honest, I was angry.

701
00:37:26,750 --> 00:37:27,890
I guess I wanted you...

702
00:37:29,660 --> 00:37:30,860
to suffer just like I was.

703
00:37:34,930 --> 00:37:37,670
Because I had such awful thoughts about you then,

704
00:37:39,700 --> 00:37:41,400
I feel like I'm the reason that happened to your child.

705
00:37:43,570 --> 00:37:44,610
Don't say that.

706
00:37:46,640 --> 00:37:47,980
It's not your fault.

707
00:37:58,190 --> 00:37:59,820
How could you even think that?

708
00:38:00,550 --> 00:38:02,390
What? What is it now?

709
00:38:02,590 --> 00:38:04,190
I heard you went to see Calvin.

710
00:38:05,190 --> 00:38:06,960
Is Calvin some kind of criminal?

711
00:38:07,830 --> 00:38:10,000
How can you even imagine something so ridiculous?

712
00:38:10,300 --> 00:38:11,970
Gosh. You called me a murderer,

713
00:38:12,030 --> 00:38:13,700
but Calvin isn't even a criminal to you?

714
00:38:14,400 --> 00:38:16,600
I didn't realise Calvin was such a wonderful person.

715
00:38:17,970 --> 00:38:21,140
In any case, you're barking up the wrong tree.

716
00:38:21,940 --> 00:38:24,810
The medication I took has nothing to do with Calvin.

717
00:38:25,950 --> 00:38:28,950
Then what is it? Stop beating around the bush...

718
00:38:29,020 --> 00:38:30,580
and just spit it out.

719
00:38:30,990 --> 00:38:33,450
What pill did you take, and how?

720
00:38:33,620 --> 00:38:34,620
That...

721
00:38:37,160 --> 00:38:38,760
Ask your friend yourself.

722
00:38:39,060 --> 00:38:40,060
What? My friend?

723
00:38:41,230 --> 00:38:43,900
I really have no idea what you're talking about.

724
00:38:48,640 --> 00:38:50,200
Okay. Let me ask you one more thing.

725
00:38:51,470 --> 00:38:53,640
Do you really still think I'm a murderer?

726
00:38:53,770 --> 00:38:54,780
The one who killed our baby?

727
00:38:59,650 --> 00:39:00,650
Then there's nothing I can do.

728
00:39:01,050 --> 00:39:02,050
I'll have to move out again.

729
00:39:03,380 --> 00:39:04,520
You're moving out again?

730
00:39:05,990 --> 00:39:07,350
Well, can you keep living in the same house...

731
00:39:07,420 --> 00:39:08,420
with a murderer like me?

732
00:39:08,760 --> 00:39:11,030
You're thrilled that I called you a murderer, aren't you?

733
00:39:11,790 --> 00:39:12,790
What?

734
00:39:12,960 --> 00:39:13,960
It's true, isn't it?

735
00:39:14,160 --> 00:39:15,330
You're using that as an excuse to move out...

736
00:39:15,960 --> 00:39:18,100
so you can live with that girl, Hee Ju.

737
00:39:18,430 --> 00:39:20,000
You pretend to be mad at me,

738
00:39:20,370 --> 00:39:21,900
but that was your real goal, wasn't it?

739
00:39:22,040 --> 00:39:23,040
Whatever.

740
00:39:23,470 --> 00:39:25,040
You'd better think about how you're going...

741
00:39:25,110 --> 00:39:26,140
to handle the consequences.

742
00:39:27,040 --> 00:39:28,310
Why would I have to deal with them?

743
00:39:28,410 --> 00:39:31,050
No, you're absolutely going to have to.

744
00:39:31,250 --> 00:39:32,880
Because I'm going to shatter this...

745
00:39:33,050 --> 00:39:34,720
ridiculous delusion of yours completely.

746
00:39:51,900 --> 00:39:53,530
What am I supposed to do now?

747
00:39:54,600 --> 00:39:56,670
I talked a big game before I left,

748
00:39:56,870 --> 00:39:59,070
but I really don't know what Mi Young is thinking.

749
00:39:59,840 --> 00:40:01,110
So, your wife...

750
00:40:01,880 --> 00:40:04,450
never told you what kind of pills they were, right?

751
00:40:05,210 --> 00:40:06,610
Right.

752
00:40:06,950 --> 00:40:10,080
She just told me to ask my friend without any details.

753
00:40:10,380 --> 00:40:13,020
She just keeps talking in riddles.

754
00:40:13,490 --> 00:40:15,820
Honestly, who else is in my life? It's just you, Kyung Tae.

755
00:40:16,790 --> 00:40:19,860
That's true. I'm your only friend.

756
00:40:20,360 --> 00:40:23,000
Anyway, it's a huge relief it wasn't from A Ri,

757
00:40:24,270 --> 00:40:26,330
but now I really don't know what to do.

758
00:40:27,130 --> 00:40:29,170
I looked into it a bit after we talked,

759
00:40:29,900 --> 00:40:33,310
and there are tons of foods to avoid during pregnancy.

760
00:40:35,310 --> 00:40:36,340
Maybe your wife...

761
00:40:37,810 --> 00:40:39,610
just wants to put the blame on you.

762
00:40:40,350 --> 00:40:41,780
If she accepts that the miscarriage is her fault,

763
00:40:43,020 --> 00:40:44,250
it would be too hard for her to bear.

764
00:40:46,190 --> 00:40:47,290
You have a point.

765
00:40:47,890 --> 00:40:50,560
Maybe you should just let this go for now...

766
00:40:51,760 --> 00:40:53,590
and finalise the lawsuit on good terms.

767
00:40:54,460 --> 00:40:55,730
Wouldn't that be better for both of you?

768
00:40:57,260 --> 00:40:58,500
You're both in the same industry,

769
00:40:59,070 --> 00:41:00,940
so you'll still be entangled even after the divorce.

770
00:41:01,000 --> 00:41:02,600
I don't want to take it this far either.

771
00:41:02,670 --> 00:41:04,870
But Baek Mi Young keeps testing me.

772
00:41:05,110 --> 00:41:06,970
Hey, she called me a murderer.

773
00:41:07,040 --> 00:41:08,740
How am I supposed to just sit back and take that?

774
00:41:08,940 --> 00:41:11,480
She probably just said that out of anger over Hee Ju.

775
00:41:12,110 --> 00:41:14,150
If you just cut ties with Hee Ju...

776
00:41:14,210 --> 00:41:15,320
This isn't about Hee Ju.

777
00:41:15,380 --> 00:41:17,280
I'm going to get to the bottom of this no matter what.

778
00:41:17,350 --> 00:41:18,750
I'll get to the bottom of it,

779
00:41:18,920 --> 00:41:21,660
and I'll prove my innocence to Baek Mi Young once and for all.

780
00:42:06,930 --> 00:42:08,240
Back when I had my miscarriage,

781
00:42:09,070 --> 00:42:11,610
I confirmed it with my doctor at the time.

782
00:42:13,310 --> 00:42:15,080
I found out that the medication my husband gave me then...

783
00:42:16,340 --> 00:42:18,180
was fatal to the fetus...

784
00:42:18,250 --> 00:42:21,050
What is this bullshit? What do you think you're doing?

785
00:42:34,360 --> 00:42:35,430
Why do you think...

786
00:42:35,960 --> 00:42:38,730
I just stood by and watched Mi Young marry a scumbag like you?

787
00:42:40,100 --> 00:42:41,840
Because Mi Young chose you.

788
00:42:42,640 --> 00:42:45,070
Because you were the one Mi Young wanted.

789
00:43:19,910 --> 00:43:20,970
Do you really not remember?

790
00:43:21,710 --> 00:43:23,210
Pills or whatever else,

791
00:43:23,280 --> 00:43:25,950
I never gave you anything that could have harmed you.

792
00:43:32,790 --> 00:43:33,790
Then there's nothing I can do.

793
00:43:34,250 --> 00:43:35,260
I'll have to move out again.

794
00:43:36,460 --> 00:43:37,620
You're moving out again?

795
00:43:38,690 --> 00:43:40,060
Well, can you keep living in the same house...

796
00:43:40,060 --> 00:43:41,330
with a murderer like me?

797
00:44:05,590 --> 00:44:08,260
(Off Air)

798
00:44:36,650 --> 00:44:37,650
It's cold.

799
00:44:39,650 --> 00:44:41,720
I'm freezing. Why isn't he here yet?

800
00:44:43,420 --> 00:44:44,420
Hey.

801
00:44:44,960 --> 00:44:46,090
Oh, come on.

802
00:44:46,860 --> 00:44:48,600
Hey. Sorry I'm a little late.

803
00:44:48,730 --> 00:44:50,800
You asked me to meet you, and you're the one who's late?

804
00:44:51,060 --> 00:44:54,470
Sorry. I promise we'll have a good time today.

805
00:44:54,670 --> 00:44:55,940
This had better be fun.

806
00:44:56,170 --> 00:44:58,140
- Let's go. - Where are we going?

807
00:44:58,210 --> 00:44:59,570
- To play a game. - What game?

808
00:44:59,910 --> 00:45:02,180
(Bowling)

809
00:45:12,050 --> 00:45:13,850
What's wrong? Are you tired?

810
00:45:14,450 --> 00:45:15,560
Yes, a little.

811
00:45:15,660 --> 00:45:17,020
This is when I'm usually fast asleep.

812
00:45:17,290 --> 00:45:18,830
That's your problem.

813
00:45:19,460 --> 00:45:21,230
When you work, you work like crazy,

814
00:45:21,460 --> 00:45:23,230
and when you rest, you sleep like a log.

815
00:45:23,530 --> 00:45:25,370
When do you ever have any fun?

816
00:45:25,430 --> 00:45:27,130
That's why I came out tonight.

817
00:45:27,730 --> 00:45:31,410
Exactly. Let's unwind for a change,

818
00:45:31,470 --> 00:45:33,270
and blow off some steam.

819
00:45:33,810 --> 00:45:35,710
- Okay? - Deal.

820
00:45:39,180 --> 00:45:41,150
They should be here any minute.

821
00:45:42,280 --> 00:45:43,280
Is someone else coming?

822
00:45:45,720 --> 00:45:47,790
Oh, wait. They're here.

823
00:45:48,560 --> 00:45:49,820
Vice President Kang, over here.

824
00:45:52,490 --> 00:45:53,490
You...

825
00:45:53,560 --> 00:45:56,400
- A Ri, I can't believe you. - Just hold on.

826
00:45:59,670 --> 00:46:01,440
- I'm leaving. - Hey, what's wrong?

827
00:46:01,500 --> 00:46:02,840
Don't be like that. Let's just have fun.

828
00:46:02,900 --> 00:46:04,470
Why would you do something I didn't ask for?

829
00:46:04,540 --> 00:46:06,010
Just one game. Please?

830
00:46:06,440 --> 00:46:07,540
Seriously.

831
00:46:09,080 --> 00:46:10,110
Come on.

832
00:46:14,010 --> 00:46:15,820
Sorry we're a little late.

833
00:46:16,020 --> 00:46:18,690
No, you're right on time.

834
00:46:19,590 --> 00:46:22,690
Great, we can make teams and get started.

835
00:46:22,760 --> 00:46:24,460
A Ri, what do you think you're doing?

836
00:46:24,990 --> 00:46:26,390
Are you really going to do this?

837
00:46:26,560 --> 00:46:27,560
I'm sorry.

838
00:46:27,830 --> 00:46:30,400
I knew you both wouldn't have come if I told you beforehand.

839
00:46:30,500 --> 00:46:32,270
- Then why did you? - You knew better, so why do this?

840
00:46:32,570 --> 00:46:34,570
Can't you two just make up?

841
00:46:35,270 --> 00:46:37,200
It's not just me. The entire J&White family...

842
00:46:37,600 --> 00:46:39,210
is walking on eggshells around you two.

843
00:46:39,570 --> 00:46:40,970
He's right.

844
00:46:41,380 --> 00:46:43,680
Let's just call today a company workshop.

845
00:46:43,740 --> 00:46:45,350
Think of it that way.

846
00:46:45,710 --> 00:46:47,850
We can play some games and build our teamwork.

847
00:46:48,350 --> 00:46:49,880
What do you say, CEO Ji?

848
00:46:51,390 --> 00:46:53,720
Well, I don't really mind, but...

849
00:46:54,890 --> 00:46:57,690
All right. Then, just like Director Song said,

850
00:46:58,590 --> 00:47:01,030
we'll think of it as a workshop.

851
00:47:02,260 --> 00:47:04,830
Great. Then shall we get started?

852
00:47:05,100 --> 00:47:06,900
The losing team buys drinks.

853
00:47:07,270 --> 00:47:08,270
Okay.

854
00:47:18,410 --> 00:47:20,210
- Okay. - Nice one.

855
00:47:32,530 --> 00:47:33,590
What was that?

856
00:47:57,920 --> 00:47:59,250
Yes!

857
00:48:00,720 --> 00:48:02,560
(Won Ho, Mi Young, Kyung Tae, A Ri)

858
00:48:18,910 --> 00:48:20,370
I told you to follow through.

859
00:48:20,540 --> 00:48:22,780
Why are you doing it like that? Do it like this.

860
00:48:25,450 --> 00:48:26,450
Fine.

861
00:48:29,150 --> 00:48:30,150
Let's go.

862
00:48:43,100 --> 00:48:44,100
Us too.

863
00:48:46,230 --> 00:48:47,230
Nice.

864
00:48:47,630 --> 00:48:49,870
Yes!

865
00:48:49,940 --> 00:48:51,170
Look at that.

866
00:48:52,740 --> 00:48:54,540
This is the last one.

867
00:48:55,910 --> 00:48:58,550
As long as Mi Young doesn't get a strike,

868
00:48:58,610 --> 00:49:00,210
we win.

869
00:49:00,280 --> 00:49:01,350
Okay, let's do this.

870
00:49:01,550 --> 00:49:03,750
- It won't be easy. - We won this.

871
00:49:03,820 --> 00:49:04,820
Baek Mi Young.

872
00:49:05,350 --> 00:49:06,350
Let's go.

873
00:49:17,130 --> 00:49:19,370
Come on...

874
00:49:20,470 --> 00:49:21,470
Okay!

875
00:49:27,010 --> 00:49:28,010
Yes!

876
00:49:29,410 --> 00:49:30,740
- Boom. Yes. - Bang!

877
00:49:32,150 --> 00:49:34,580
- Cheers, everyone. - Cheers.

878
00:49:41,860 --> 00:49:43,120
Goodness.

879
00:49:44,160 --> 00:49:46,190
Another beer over here.

880
00:49:46,560 --> 00:49:49,000
Gosh, Director Song. You're really going for it tonight.

881
00:49:49,560 --> 00:49:51,260
Are you okay?

882
00:49:51,500 --> 00:49:53,600
Of course.

883
00:49:53,670 --> 00:49:55,640
I'm Song A Ri.

884
00:49:55,800 --> 00:49:59,470
A little beer is nothing.

885
00:49:59,710 --> 00:50:01,440
We can tell you're really drunk.

886
00:50:01,840 --> 00:50:02,840
You should stop drinking now.

887
00:50:02,910 --> 00:50:06,080
You can tell I'm not drunk at all.

888
00:50:08,820 --> 00:50:10,180
Where are we?

889
00:50:11,180 --> 00:50:12,690
What round is this?

890
00:50:12,750 --> 00:50:13,750
What?

891
00:50:14,290 --> 00:50:16,520
Director Song, let's call it a night.

892
00:50:17,120 --> 00:50:19,130
I'll get Director Song a taxi and be right back.

893
00:50:19,460 --> 00:50:20,630
Can you manage on your own?

894
00:50:21,090 --> 00:50:23,100
- Should I go with you? - No, it's fine.

895
00:50:23,500 --> 00:50:25,570
You two can talk while I'm gone.

896
00:50:25,770 --> 00:50:26,800
Let's go, Director Song.

897
00:50:26,800 --> 00:50:28,240
- Let's go. - Are we going to round three?

898
00:50:28,300 --> 00:50:29,300
- Come on, let's go. - Goodness.

899
00:50:29,370 --> 00:50:30,940
- Nice! - Come on, we have to go.

900
00:50:31,000 --> 00:50:32,770
- Let's go for round four. - Careful.

901
00:50:32,840 --> 00:50:33,910
We have to make it to round four.

902
00:50:45,950 --> 00:50:46,990
Come back home.

903
00:50:49,060 --> 00:50:52,030
- Are you serious? - You can't keep living in a motel.

904
00:50:52,460 --> 00:50:54,490
It's not like I intentionally kicked you out.

905
00:50:55,060 --> 00:50:57,130
Then what about when you called me a murderer?

906
00:50:57,760 --> 00:50:58,870
Are you taking that back too?

907
00:50:59,600 --> 00:51:00,600
What?

908
00:51:00,730 --> 00:51:02,970
There has to be a reason you're suddenly acting like this.

909
00:51:03,300 --> 00:51:05,310
Have you cleared up your misunderstandings about me?

910
00:51:05,540 --> 00:51:08,070
Does this mean I don't have to hear about those pills anymore?

911
00:51:08,740 --> 00:51:09,740
About the pills?

912
00:51:13,510 --> 00:51:15,220
If you don't want to come home, then don't.

913
00:51:15,380 --> 00:51:17,720
Just keep living at the motel and fooling around with Hee Ju.

914
00:51:17,850 --> 00:51:19,290
Are you messing with me right now?

915
00:51:19,350 --> 00:51:20,850
Why do you keep going back and forth?

916
00:51:20,920 --> 00:51:23,490
And why can't you get it through your thick skull?

917
00:51:23,560 --> 00:51:26,290
What did you just say? Hey, are you done?

918
00:51:26,360 --> 00:51:28,090
I'm done. You look like you're about to hit me.

919
00:51:28,160 --> 00:51:29,300
Go on, hit me.

920
00:51:29,500 --> 00:51:31,800
Here. Is this what you want? Happy now?

921
00:51:31,870 --> 00:51:35,140
- Fine. Do whatever you want. - It hurts. My head hurts.

922
00:51:37,740 --> 00:51:39,570
Why are you two acting like this?

923
00:51:42,680 --> 00:51:44,540
You promised to part with a smile.

924
00:51:46,480 --> 00:51:47,480
This won't do.

925
00:51:47,950 --> 00:51:49,450
I'll just have to force you to smile.

926
00:51:50,320 --> 00:51:51,320
Excuse me, ma'am.

927
00:51:52,790 --> 00:51:55,090
Sorry to bother you, but could you take a picture for us?

928
00:51:55,160 --> 00:51:56,520
Why are we suddenly taking a picture?

929
00:51:56,520 --> 00:51:58,530
Won Ho, get in closer. Mi Young, closer.

930
00:51:58,590 --> 00:52:00,260
Okay, everyone, look over there and smile.

931
00:52:00,490 --> 00:52:03,130
Okay, I'm taking the picture. One, two, three.

932
00:52:11,470 --> 00:52:13,270
You and Mi Young should share a taxi.

933
00:52:14,510 --> 00:52:15,510
What are you talking about?

934
00:52:15,910 --> 00:52:18,280
Hurry and go make things right with Mi Young.

935
00:52:22,780 --> 00:52:25,220
- Go on. Hurry up. - Unbelievable.

936
00:52:33,290 --> 00:52:34,290
Hey.

937
00:52:35,030 --> 00:52:38,060
- Oh my gosh, are you okay? - Darn it.

938
00:52:38,370 --> 00:52:39,470
- Are you okay? - Darn it.

939
00:52:39,530 --> 00:52:40,530
What happened?

940
00:52:40,600 --> 00:52:42,700
My coat got caught in the door, and I was trying to pull it out...

941
00:52:43,170 --> 00:52:44,240
Are you okay? What do I do?

942
00:52:44,300 --> 00:52:46,740
- Go, just go. - You should go, Mi Young.

943
00:52:46,810 --> 00:52:48,110
I'll take him home.

944
00:52:48,480 --> 00:52:49,780
I'm so sorry.

945
00:52:56,050 --> 00:52:57,850
Hey, let me see. Does it hurt a lot?

946
00:52:58,250 --> 00:52:59,620
Of course it hurts!

947
00:53:00,850 --> 00:53:01,860
Does it hurt that much?

948
00:53:02,320 --> 00:53:03,760
(Calvin)

949
00:53:08,560 --> 00:53:10,960
- Hello? - You must still be sleeping.

950
00:53:12,230 --> 00:53:14,170
What? Why are you calling?

951
00:53:15,240 --> 00:53:16,470
You didn't find the evidence, did you?

952
00:53:17,100 --> 00:53:18,370
I'm about to find it.

953
00:53:18,510 --> 00:53:20,010
I have the evidence.

954
00:53:20,740 --> 00:53:24,080
- What? - You have neither ability nor will.

955
00:53:24,740 --> 00:53:27,380
I figured you'd just go around stirring up trouble.

956
00:53:27,880 --> 00:53:29,580
So I just found the evidence myself.

957
00:53:31,550 --> 00:53:33,850
I'll give you two hours. Come and get it.

958
00:53:39,790 --> 00:53:40,990
It's just the angle...

959
00:53:41,360 --> 00:53:42,560
Why? Is there a problem?

960
00:53:42,730 --> 00:53:44,230
It looks like they're kissing, but...

961
00:53:44,730 --> 00:53:46,200
it wasn't captured very well on camera.

962
00:53:46,600 --> 00:53:47,800
I see that.

963
00:53:48,700 --> 00:53:51,200
If that couple comes again, I'll let you know.

964
00:53:51,770 --> 00:53:52,770
Thank you.

965
00:53:57,680 --> 00:53:58,680
But...

966
00:53:59,110 --> 00:54:01,350
I feel bad that I keep getting your help.

967
00:54:01,720 --> 00:54:04,150
Not at all. I do it because I want to.

968
00:54:05,650 --> 00:54:07,890
You want to?

969
00:54:14,930 --> 00:54:16,230
You cut your hair.

970
00:54:16,400 --> 00:54:18,000
It looks really good on you.

971
00:54:18,060 --> 00:54:19,270
It's pretty. Very pretty.

972
00:54:19,600 --> 00:54:21,630
- It's pretty? - Yes.

973
00:54:29,640 --> 00:54:31,080
Oh, right. There's something...

974
00:54:31,140 --> 00:54:33,210
I'd like to ask for your legal advice on.

975
00:54:33,680 --> 00:54:34,680
Yes.

976
00:54:35,420 --> 00:54:37,620
If you have any questions, feel free to ask me anything.

977
00:54:37,750 --> 00:54:42,960
Yes. How would I remove a guest from their room?

978
00:54:43,020 --> 00:54:44,590
Are you talking about a forced eviction?

979
00:54:44,760 --> 00:54:47,060
Yes, a forced eviction. How do I make that happen?

980
00:54:47,860 --> 00:54:49,630
If they're a wanted fugitive on the run...

981
00:54:49,700 --> 00:54:51,330
or if they've caused property damage,

982
00:54:51,400 --> 00:54:52,970
like vandalizing things in the room, you can.

983
00:54:54,000 --> 00:54:56,740
What if the guest is just a bad person?

984
00:54:56,800 --> 00:54:59,140
Would that be considered grounds for a forced eviction?

985
00:54:59,440 --> 00:55:00,610
A bad person?

986
00:55:01,670 --> 00:55:03,010
That's a bit of a gray area.

987
00:55:03,680 --> 00:55:04,680
Why?

988
00:55:04,840 --> 00:55:07,150
Is there a problem guest in this building?

989
00:55:07,410 --> 00:55:10,020
We offered a full refund, but they're refusing to leave,

990
00:55:10,180 --> 00:55:11,620
and they're threatening my mother and me.

991
00:55:11,820 --> 00:55:12,820
Threatening you?

992
00:55:13,720 --> 00:55:14,720
That person over there.

993
00:55:15,790 --> 00:55:17,820
- Excuse me, miss. - Ahn Hee Ju.

994
00:55:18,790 --> 00:55:19,790
Yes?

995
00:55:30,700 --> 00:55:31,700
A lawyer?

996
00:55:32,310 --> 00:55:33,970
Right now, my client is...

997
00:55:37,480 --> 00:55:38,980
It's Ahn Hee Ju.

998
00:55:40,680 --> 00:55:43,320
On the verge of pressing charges against you, Ahn Hee Ju.

999
00:55:43,680 --> 00:55:44,680
Press charges?

1000
00:55:49,460 --> 00:55:50,460
What is this?

1001
00:55:50,920 --> 00:55:53,060
I heard you threatened the owner.

1002
00:55:53,760 --> 00:55:57,060
- What? - Why do you insist on staying?

1003
00:55:58,800 --> 00:56:00,530
What is your reason for insisting on this specific motel?

1004
00:56:01,400 --> 00:56:04,370
Look. I'm a little busy right now.

1005
00:56:05,410 --> 00:56:08,140
I'll talk to you next time we meet.

1006
00:56:08,540 --> 00:56:10,140
You don't look that busy to me.

1007
00:56:10,380 --> 00:56:12,510
I'm on my way to catch a murderer.

1008
00:56:14,010 --> 00:56:15,010
A murderer?

1009
00:56:15,080 --> 00:56:16,480
If I let them get away,

1010
00:56:17,180 --> 00:56:18,690
are you going to catch them for me?

1011
00:56:22,160 --> 00:56:23,160
Gosh.

1012
00:56:26,930 --> 00:56:27,930
See what I mean?

1013
00:56:28,190 --> 00:56:31,030
She's a rotten person.

1014
00:56:31,970 --> 00:56:32,970
A what?

1015
00:56:33,530 --> 00:56:35,500
Oh, I said, rotten.

1016
00:56:36,840 --> 00:56:40,140
You're right. She is a completely rotten person.

1017
00:56:40,140 --> 00:56:41,210
Yes.

1018
00:56:46,110 --> 00:56:49,920
Take it. Icing it might help it heal faster.

1019
00:56:51,720 --> 00:56:54,490
It's a good thing you weren't cut.

1020
00:56:55,090 --> 00:56:56,920
Are you worried about me?

1021
00:56:57,960 --> 00:56:58,960
I'm going to go.

1022
00:56:59,390 --> 00:57:01,090
Can't you just tell me straight?

1023
00:57:10,140 --> 00:57:12,310
I'm talking about the pills you said you took three years ago.

1024
00:57:13,510 --> 00:57:16,110
Can't you stop being evasive and just tell me what happened?

1025
00:57:17,510 --> 00:57:19,650
I need to hear what on earth those pills you took were,

1026
00:57:19,710 --> 00:57:21,750
and why you keep calling me a murderer.

1027
00:57:21,810 --> 00:57:24,380
I need you to tell me first before I decide what to do.

1028
00:57:25,350 --> 00:57:26,350
Decide?

1029
00:57:26,590 --> 00:57:28,790
Whether I should keep denying it,

1030
00:57:31,490 --> 00:57:32,560
or if I should truly apologize...

1031
00:57:32,560 --> 00:57:34,660
and beg for your forgiveness on my knees.

1032
00:57:34,830 --> 00:57:36,200
You would beg for forgiveness?

1033
00:57:36,330 --> 00:57:37,360
If it really was my fault,

1034
00:57:37,460 --> 00:57:40,070
I'll admit it, no questions asked, and beg for your forgiveness.

1035
00:57:43,670 --> 00:57:44,670
So just tell me.

1036
00:57:45,840 --> 00:57:46,970
On that day three years ago,

1037
00:57:48,010 --> 00:57:49,540
what exactly were those pills you took?

1038
00:57:55,080 --> 00:57:56,220
No, wait...

1039
00:57:57,150 --> 00:57:58,150
Why is this person...

1040
00:57:58,650 --> 00:57:59,650
Are you disappointed...

1041
00:58:00,250 --> 00:58:03,360
that I wasn't the one who pushed you off the cliff?

1042
00:58:04,060 --> 00:58:05,060
Is this...

1043
00:58:06,260 --> 00:58:07,260
real?

1044
00:58:07,890 --> 00:58:09,060
You didn't fake this, did you?

1045
00:58:09,400 --> 00:58:11,030
If you're curious, go check for yourself.

1046
00:58:12,000 --> 00:58:14,030
Around the time you fell from the cliff,

1047
00:58:14,100 --> 00:58:15,640
within 30 minutes before and after,

1048
00:58:16,000 --> 00:58:17,870
only one person came down...

1049
00:58:18,570 --> 00:58:20,710
to the parking lot, besides the couple...

1050
00:58:20,770 --> 00:58:21,770
doing their wedding shoot.

1051
00:58:23,580 --> 00:58:24,580
That person.

1052
00:58:28,450 --> 00:58:30,180
This is as far as I can help you.

1053
00:58:31,420 --> 00:58:33,320
Whether you want revenge or retribution,

1054
00:58:33,850 --> 00:58:35,050
the rest is up to you.

1055
00:58:35,560 --> 00:58:36,790
It's none of my business.

1056
00:58:39,590 --> 00:58:42,300
I just don't understand why I should have to explain...

1057
00:58:42,530 --> 00:58:44,330
this to you.

1058
00:58:45,370 --> 00:58:46,700
Okay, I'm sorry too.

1059
00:58:47,270 --> 00:58:49,100
I'm sorry for the fact...

1060
00:58:49,740 --> 00:58:52,740
that you resent me this much, and I still have no idea why.

1061
00:58:53,640 --> 00:58:54,810
So, Mi Young.

1062
00:58:55,640 --> 00:58:57,410
Please, just tell me now.

1063
00:58:58,040 --> 00:59:00,580
What were the pills that gave you such a hard time?

1064
00:59:01,110 --> 00:59:03,620
I need to hear it directly from you, okay?

1065
00:59:12,290 --> 00:59:14,190
What put Dallae in danger was...

1066
00:59:15,360 --> 00:59:16,600
the herbal medicine.

1067
00:59:17,400 --> 00:59:18,870
Not the pills from Calvin.

1068
00:59:19,470 --> 00:59:20,470
Herbal medicine?

1069
00:59:26,370 --> 00:59:27,540
You really don't remember?

1070
00:59:29,110 --> 00:59:31,540
The one you asked Kyung Tae to get.

1071
00:59:33,850 --> 00:59:34,850
Kyung Tae?

1072
01:00:31,440 --> 01:00:34,410
(OK! Let's Get Divorced)

1073
01:00:34,970 --> 01:00:36,580
It's been three years. What's the point now?

1074
01:00:36,640 --> 01:00:38,880
So that you can finally show some remorse and apologize.

1075
01:00:39,350 --> 01:00:40,450
What difference would that make?

1076
01:00:40,580 --> 01:00:42,150
So that was today...

1077
01:00:43,520 --> 01:00:44,520
Time flies.

1078
01:00:45,150 --> 01:00:46,820
You know what's really upsetting?

1079
01:00:47,690 --> 01:00:50,560
It's the fact that my husband has already forgotten all about it.

1080
01:00:51,760 --> 01:00:54,030
That brooch Mi Young lost...

1081
01:00:54,090 --> 01:00:56,130
I'd like to ask you something about this.

1082
01:00:56,600 --> 01:00:58,560
